00:11:24.039 --> 00:11:31.320
and you only assess a certain part, but in general, you sit down with the model owners or

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:37.479
the people who own the model. You ask them to give you all the documentation. So you study the models,

00:11:37.479 --> 00:11:40.520
you ask a lot of questions. So the first stage is like a research stage.

00:11:41.159 --> 00:11:46.119
Once you have your ideas, you can either ask them to stress test, to see all the validations that

00:11:46.119 --> 00:11:50.679
the first line of defense has done. And then because you have done many of these validations,

00:11:50.679 --> 00:11:55.719
you have your own list of tests like parameters. What happens if you change this parameter?

00:11:55.719 --> 00:12:01.159
What happens if you change your model assumptions? If you use a different model,

00:12:02.039 --> 00:12:07.159
where do you get the data? Is the data fit for purpose? Are the risks you're analyzing material

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:12.840
or are there any blind spots? So a model validation contains many, many different

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:20.039
aspects, but the main piece is, is the design of the model reasonable? And are the parameters

00:12:20.039 --> 00:12:25.000
